ral Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-12\nValid as Of: 2023-12-12\nVersion: 2310\n\n--- Record 3747 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Core SDK\nDescription: You can now use the Get Screen Application Instance Count activity to return the number of instances of the application screen and the Get Screen Application Instance (Index) activity to retrieve the instance of the application screen from its index.  For more information, see Core SDK.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-12\nValid as Of: 2023-12-12\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3748 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Create and Manage Projects\nDescription: User principles are now case insensitive. For example, \"user@mail.com\" is treated as the same entity as \"USER@mAil.cOM\".\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest", "-12-12\nValid as Of: 2023-12-12\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3748 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Create and Manage Projects\nDescription: User principles are now case insensitive. For example, \"user@mail.com\" is treated as the same entity as \"USER@mAil.cOM\".\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-12\nValid as Of: 2023-12-12\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3749 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Different Types of Set Activity Options in the Enhanced Recorder\nDescription: You can now use the following options in the enhanced recorder to modify the input value for the Set activity.    Convert Input into a Variable - This option allows you to convert an input value into a variable.  Replace Variable with Original Input - This option allows you to replace a variable with the original input value.  Replace Input with Existing Variable - This option allows you to replace an input value with the pre-existing variable.    For more information, see Different Types of Set Activity Options in the Enhanced Recorder.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-12\nValid as Of: 2023-12-12\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3750 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Error Management in the Enhanced Recorder\nDescription: You can now effectively manage errors that may arise while recording in the enhanced recorder. For more information, see Error Management in the Enhanced Recorder.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-12\nValid as Of: 2023-12-12\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 4141 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Define Custom Variables for Your Process\nDescription: You can define variables that are available on a global level of the process. That is, these variables do not stem from a previous process activity. You use them to provide input, for example, for an activity that follows conditional branches.  See Configure Process Variables.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-09-28\nValid as Of: 2023-09-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4142 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Input Validation in Forms\nDescription: In the form editor, you can configure input validation for the text fields in the form you create. For more information, see Form Input Fields.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-09-28\nValid as Of: 2023-09-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4143 ---\nComponent: SAP Java Buildpack\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Interface com.sap.xsa.security.container.XSUserInfo has been deprecated\nDescription: With SAP Java Buildpack 1.77.0, component xs-user-holder is changed due to deprecated code in SAP BTP Security Services Integration Libraries, on which it relies.  Interface com.sap.xsa.security.container.XSUserInfo was deprecated and later removed with version 3.0.0 of cloud-security-services-integration-library. For more information, see: SAP BTP Security Services Integration Libraries: v 3.0.0  This interface is replaced by a new one – com.sap.xs.security.UserData. It's introduced with version 1.47.0 of xs-user-holder.   If your pom.xml file contains the following <dependency>, that means your project uses xs-user-holder and needs to be adapted:   <dependency>\n    <groupId>com.sap.cloud.sjb</groupId>\n    <artifactId>xs-user-holder</artifactId>\n</dependency>\n  The xs-user-holder component currently provides getter and setter methods for working with the deprecated com.sap.xsa.security.container.XSUserInfo.   Action: If your code uses these methods, make the following modifications:      Replace UserInfoHolder.getUserInfo() with UserInfoHolder.getUserData()      Replace UserInfoHolder.setUserInfo(XSUserInfo userInfo) with UserInfoHolder.setUserData(UserData userData)      Note      The same token information that XSUserInfo provides can be obtained with the new UserData interface.      Getter and setter methods for the deprecated com.sap.xsa.security.container.XSUserInfo will remain available in the xs-user-holder component, and will coexist with the methods from com.sap.xs.security.UserData till December 31, 2023.      When this period is over, everything based on the deprecated code from package com.sap.xsa.security.container will be removed, and only the new UserData interface will be supported in the xs-user-holder component.    \nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-09-15\nValid as Of: 2023-09-27\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4144 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Corporate IdP\nDescription: Identity Authentication added new parameter idp which allows sign in to specific application with specific corporate identity provider. See Configure the Client to Call Identity Authentication Authorize Endpoint for Authorization Code Flowand Configure IdP-Initiated SSO.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-09-28\nValid as Of: 2023-09-27\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4145 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Regular Upgrade\nDescription: Identity Authentication has been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-09-28\nValid as Of: 2023-09-27\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4146 ---\nComponent: Cloud Management Tools,SAP BTP Cockpit\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo,Other\nTitle: Directory Enhancements for Managing Users and Entitlements\nDescription: Directories are primarily used for grouping your subaccounts, but they can also be used to manage their own entitlements and users. Previously, enabling the entitlement and user management features for a directory was only possible after the directory was created, from the directory's Users and Entitlements pages.   Now, we've made it easier for you to enable these features right from the start when you create a directory, or when editing a directory from the Account Explorer page.  Furthermore, we've added the ability to enable the entitlement management feature for any directory directly on the global account's Entitlements  Entity Entitlements page. Until now, this page did not allow you to select directories that weren't enabled to manage entitlements. Now, these directories can be selected.  For more information, see Entitlements and Quotas, Create a Directory, Configure Entitlements and Quotas for Directories, and Manage Users in Directories.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-09-27\nValid as Of: 2023-09-27\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4147 ---\nComponent: Data Quality Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Enh", " see Entitlements and Quotas, Create a Directory, Configure Entitlements and Quotas for Directories, and Manage Users in Directories.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-09-27\nValid as Of: 2023-09-27\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4147 ---\nComponent: Data Quality Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Enhancements\nDescription: When sending a request with type ahead suggestions enabled and the value for the country input field property is United States, the microservice now searches for the address in the United States and its territories.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2023-09-27\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4148 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: SAP SuccessFactors version 2 - implement group prefix\nDescription: The group prefix mechanism that is used for distinguishing groups of a given provisioning system is now implemented for SAP SuccessFactors version 2 using SAP SuccessFactors Workforce SCIM API.  For more information, see List of Properties → sf.group.prefix.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-06\nValid as Of: 2023-09-27\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4149 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Updated business partner roles for SAP S/4 HANA-based systems\nDescription: The default transformati